<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the packaged app. electron-builder applies
  this file to the main app AND the nested Electron helpers (entitlements and
  entitlementsInherit both point here — the sandbox-style "inherit" plist is
  the wrong tool under hardened runtime).

  - allow-jit: V8 JIT under hardened runtime (main process and renderer
    helpers).
  - allow-unsigned-executable-memory: Electron still allocates executable
    memory outside the MAP_JIT path in places; without it hardened-runtime
    builds can crash at startup.

  Deliberately omitted from electron-builder's default template:
  com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation. Our native modules
  (better-sqlite3, node-pty + its spawn-helper, all in app.asar.unpacked) are
  signed with the same Developer ID by electron-builder's deep-sign pass, so
  library validation holds without it. If a future native dep ships pre-signed
  by a third party and fails to dlopen, this is the knob to revisit.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
